On Mon, 2011-01-17, Pat Rankin wrote:
> On Jan 15, 5:48 pm, Andrew Fabbro <andrew.fab...@gmail.com> wrote:
>> I followed the recipe on Wikihack to build Nethack 3.4.3. on Linux:
> [ obsolete url already addressed in a previous reply ]
>>
>> Everything went fine but nethack refuses to display any colors.  I
>> have in my ~/.nethackrc:
>> OPTIONS=windowtype:tty
>> OPTIONS=color
>>
>> The only things I changed in the build (other than what's in the
>> Wikihack recipe) were to turn on AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTIONS and DLB.
>>
>> Is there something else I need to do in order to get color?
>
>      You need to run nethack from a color terminal.
> Presumably your environment has set TERM to "xterm" or
> some other value that is considered to be monochrome.
> Even though it is capable of displaying color, its
> termcap or terminfo definition doesn't say so, and
> nethack is going by that.  Try changing TERM to be
> "xterm-color" before running nethack.  If that doesn't
> work, some other magic value is needed.

I get the feeling that "xterm" today includes the color capability. I
haven't set $TERM to xterm-color for many years, and yet many programs
come in colors. (Maybe they ignore the terminal settings.)

